Architecture and design notes
-----------------------------

The following projects informed the architecture and interaction design of
this software. No source code was copied from them; the implementations here
are original. They are acknowledged because ideas are worth crediting.

  * Parallax (MIT License)
    - Bridge abstraction pattern (one UI, multiple backends)
    - Provider adapter + preset configuration structure
    - The insight that streaming deltas must be batched before hitting the UI

  * Cherry Studio (AGPL-3.0)
    - Product-level interaction and information-architecture references only.
      No code from this project is used, and none may be incorporated without
      adopting the AGPL-3.0 license for the whole of this work.

  * Cline (Apache-2.0)
    - Approval-tier model for tool risk levels
    - Checkpointing approach for workspace snapshots

  * LangGraph (MIT License)
    - Durable-execution vocabulary: interrupt, resume, checkpoint

  * OpenHands (MIT License)
    - Event-stream representation of agent activity

  * Temporal (MIT License)
    - Terminology for retries, idempotency keys and workflow versioning

